Original commit body from a4aa5fd:

Adds a new language convention pattern file that detects test functions
across multiple languages and frameworks:

- Python: pytest/unittest test_* functions, @pytest.fixture
- Go: Test*, Benchmark*, Example* functions
- Java/Kotlin: @Test, @BeforeEach, @AfterEach, @ParameterizedTest
- JavaScript/TypeScript: test* functions (jest/mocha/vitest)
- Ruby: test_* methods (Minitest)
- Rust: #[test], #[bench] attributes
- C#: [Test], [Fact], [Theory], [TestMethod] (NUnit/xUnit/MSTest)
- Swift: test* methods, setUp/tearDown (XCTest)
- PHP: test* methods, @test annotation (PHPUnit)

The patterns use decorator matching for annotation-based frameworks
and symbol_name matching for naming convention-based frameworks.
This enables filtering test code from production code in slices.

Also updates enrich_symbols() to always load test-frameworks.yaml
alongside main-functions.yaml for language convention detection.
